{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLzHCgwR3SZoMwDupfde","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GmUe5XB1VTFVHaqrNVXCGp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-27-responses-adapter/.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec; sed -n 560,624p 06-llm-protocols.md; sed -n 958,1100p 06-llm-protocols.md | grep -n -i -B2 -A6 'respons'"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5894,"cache_read_input_tokens":71094,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5894},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3b53f31-1a37-4344-81e1-3cd017cb5d08","uuid":"940332df-5cd8-49fc-9036-2c8646a3c458","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:46:48.763Z","request_id":"req_011ChLzHCPpyFRPJJimusKU9","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GmUe5XB1VTFVHaqrNVXCGp":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-27-responses-adapter/.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec; sed -n 560,624p 06-llm-protocols.md; sed -n 958,1100p 06-llm-protocols.md | grep -n -i -B2 -A6 'respons'"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GmUe5XB1VTFVHaqrNVXCGp","type":"tool_result","content":"   provider error `type`/`code` and `message` parsed best-effort from\n   `{\"error\":{\"type\",\"code\",\"message\"}}` or Anthropic's\n   `{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\",\"message\"}}`. Retryable when any of:\n   header `x-should-retry` is one of Go `ParseBool`'s true spellings (`1`,\n   `t`, `T`, `true`, `TRUE`, `True`); status `408`, `409`, `429`, or\n   `>= 500`. A false `x-should-retry` does not prevent a status-based\n   retry.\n   `401`, `403`, other 4xx, and 3xx are not retryable.\n2. **Stream error**: an error delivered inside a 200 stream (chat `error`\n   member, Anthropic `error` event). Retryable iff the provider error\n   `type` (or `code` when type is empty) is one of `server_error`,\n   `internal_error`, `overloaded_error`, `api_error`, `rate_limit_error`.\n   Responses `response.failed` / `error` events are never retryable.\n3. **Incomplete stream**: the body ended cleanly without the protocol's\n   terminal signal (2.8). Message `stream transport error: unexpected EOF`.\n   Retryable.\n4. **Transport error**: `fetch` rejected or the body read failed for a\n   network reason (connection refused/reset, DNS failure, socket closed,\n   TLS failure, HTTP/2 stream reset, unexpected EOF mid-body). Retryable.\n5. **Abort**: the request's `AbortSignal` fired (caller cancellation, the\n   agent loop's work deadline, or the per-request timeout). Never retried.\n   The adapter rethrows the signal's reason unchanged so the caller can tell\n   them apart.\n6. **Capture error** (2.11). Permanent; never retried, and it disables\n   the client.\n7. **Protocol error**: malformed event JSON, a non-`function` chat tool\n   call type. Not retryable.\n\nRetry delay hints (consumed by the agent loop's retry policy, which owns\nthe loop: up to `maxAttempts` attempts per model call, Go Fantasy\n`DefaultRetryOptions` initial delay 5000 ms, factor 2, so 5 s, 10 s, 20 s):\nfor an HTTP error with headers, `retry-after-ms` (float milliseconds), else\n`retry-after` (float seconds, or an RFC 1123 date relative to now) gives\n`hint`; the delay is `hint` when `hint > 0` and (`hint < 60 s` or `hint <\nbackoff`), otherwise the exponential backoff. Adapters never retry\ninternally (Go disables SDK retries: a 500 with `maxAttempts: 1` reaches\nthe server exactly once).\n\n`normalizeProviderError(outerSignal, model, err)` maps any error that\nescapes the agent loop, in this order:\n\n1. `outerSignal.aborted` -> return `outerSignal.reason` (caller\n   cancellation passes through untouched).\n2. `err` is an abort or timeout (request timeout, work-deadline-bounded\n   call) -> `ErrEndpoint` with message\n   `llm: inference endpoint failure: <model>: <err message>`, keeping the\n   timeout as `cause` (pinned: a request timeout is an endpoint failure that\n   still identifies as a deadline).\n3. `err` already is `ErrAuth`, `ErrEndpoint`, or `ErrBudgetExhausted`\n   (ledger area) -> unchanged.\n4. `err` carries HTTP status 401 or 403 anywhere in its cause chain ->\n   `ErrAuth`: `llm: authentication failed: <err message>; check the\n   configured API key`.\n5. Otherwise -> `ErrEndpoint` as in step 2.\n\nSentinel kinds (Go `errors.go`) become error classes with a `kind` field\nso callers test `err instanceof AuthError` or walk `cause`:\n`ErrNoFinalCall` (`llm: tool loop ended without a final tool call`),\n`ErrWorkDeadline` (`llm: work deadline reached`), `ErrAuth`\n(`llm: authentication failed`), `ErrEndpoint`\n(`llm: inference endpoint failure`). The first two are raised by the agent\nloop; they are defined here so the whole `llm` error vocabulary lives in\none module.\n\n### 2.11 Raw response capture\n8-pure unit tests for the SSE parser, usage normalization and encoders.\n9-A shared fixture writer ports `testutil.WriteInferenceStream`: from a\n10:complete response object it emits the native SSE sequence for each\n11:protocol (chat chunks plus `[DONE]`; responses events with\n12-`sequence_number`; anthropic `message_start` ... `message_stop`).\n13-\n14-Wire shape and headers:\n15-\n16-- Anthropic posts to `<base>/v1/messages` after `/v1` trimming, sends\n17-  `X-Api-Key`, a non-empty `Anthropic-Version`, `system`, `stream: true`,\n--\n23-- Anthropic and structured calls use `tool_choice.type == \"auto\"`\n24-  (`TestAnthropicCompleteStructuredUsesAutomaticToolChoice`) (C).\n25:- Responses replays `function_call_output`, sends `store: false`, no\n26:  `previous_response_id`, `tool_choice: \"auto\"`, identical tools on the\n27:  final turn (`TestResponsesAgentReplaysToolOutputAndKeepsToolsOnFinalTurn`)\n28-  (C).\n29-- Tool schemas reach each protocol with `additionalProperties` and nested\n30-  `required` lists intact\n31-  (`TestToolSchemasCarryRequiredFields`) (C).\n32-- `User-Agent` is `roast/<version>` (`TestUserAgentIncludesBuildVersion`)\n33-  (U on the header builder).\n34-- Chat `max_completion_tokens` for reasoning-model IDs, `max_tokens`\n35:  otherwise; responses system mode by model (no Go test; new) (U).\n36-\n37-Ambient environment and credentials:\n38-\n39-- For each protocol and each env scenario (provider keys, auth token,\n40-  explicit and fallback Anthropic profile, federation, custom headers),\n41-  only the configured endpoint is called, once, with only Roast headers\n--\n45-- Anthropic 401 maps to `AuthError`\n46-  (`TestAnthropicMapsAuthenticationFailure`) (C, exit code and JSON).\n47:- A 3xx from any protocol (`chat`, `responses`, `anthropic`) is not\n48-  followed, the target sees no key, and the error is an `EndpointError`,\n49-  not retried (`TestAnthropicDoesNotForwardCredentialsThroughRedirect`,\n50-  extended) (A).\n51-- An error body larger than 32 KiB is read only up to 32768 bytes (new)\n52-  (A).\n53-\n--\n69-  (C via a run-record write failure, or A).\n70-- `Content-Length: 16777217` fails with the size error\n71:  (`TestCaptureRejectsOversizedProviderResponse`) (A).\n72-- Invalid JSON 2xx body fails once, not retried\n73:  (`TestCaptureDoesNotRetryInvalidJSONResponse`) (A).\n74-- Streaming capture does not read ahead, preserves exactly the bytes read,\n75-  releases the body once (`TestStreamCaptureDoesNotEagerlyReadAndPreserves\n76-  PartialBytes`) (A with a controlled `ReadableStream`).\n77-- No `Content-Length`: overflow fails, callback not called, buffer never\n78-  exceeds the cap (`TestStreamCaptureEnforcesLimitWithoutContentLength`)\n79-  (U on `capture.ts`).\n--\n82-  completed calls\n83-  (`TestAnthropicInterruptedStreamRetriesWithoutExecutingPartialTools`)\n84:  (C, run-record raw responses).\n85-\n86-Retries and errors:\n87-\n88-- A 500 with `maxAttempts: 1` reaches the server once for chat and\n89:  responses (`TestChatRetriesOnlyThroughFantasy`,\n90:  `TestResponsesRetriesOnlyThroughFantasy`) (C).\n91-- Request timeout yields `EndpointError` caused by a timeout within one\n92-  second (`TestInferenceRequestTimeoutIsEndpointFailure`) (A).\n93-- Classification table: 408/409/429/5xx/`x-should-retry` retryable,\n94-  401/403/3xx/400 not, transient stream types, incomplete stream,\n95-  transport errors, aborts (new) (U).\n96-- `retryDelayMs` with `retry-after-ms`, `retry-after` seconds and date,\n--\n103-- Stage 2 on 8/4/1/3 -> 8/4/1/3 (`TestGenericUsageAccounting`, updated)\n104-  (U).\n105:- Chat and responses from fixture usage objects: `prompt_tokens: 100,\n106-  cached_tokens: 30` -> uncached 70, cached 30; cached 80 -> 20 and 80 (new)\n107-  (U).\n108-- A chat chunk without usage after a chunk with usage keeps the earlier\n109-  usage (new) (U).\n110-- `encodeToolResult` sorts keys and leaves `<>&` and U+2028 unescaped; a\n111-  lone surrogate in model output decodes to U+FFFD (new) (U).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3b53f31-1a37-4344-81e1-3cd017cb5d08","uuid":"225a6501-48ec-4787-844c-14074295243f","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:46:48.890Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"   provider error `type`/`code` and `message` parsed best-effort from\n   `{\"error\":{\"type\",\"code\",\"message\"}}` or Anthropic's\n   `{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\",\"message\"}}`. Retryable when any of:\n   header `x-should-retry` is one of Go `ParseBool`'s true spellings (`1`,\n   `t`, `T`, `true`, `TRUE`, `True`); status `408`, `409`, `429`, or\n   `>= 500`. A false `x-should-retry` does not prevent a status-based\n   retry.\n   `401`, `403`, other 4xx, and 3xx are not retryable.\n2. **Stream error**: an error delivered inside a 200 stream (chat `error`\n   member, Anthropic `error` event). Retryable iff the provider error\n   `type` (or `code` when type is empty) is one of `server_error`,\n   `internal_error`, `overloaded_error`, `api_error`, `rate_limit_error`.\n   Responses `response.failed` / `error` events are never retryable.\n3. **Incomplete stream**: the body ended cleanly without the protocol's\n   terminal signal (2.8). Message `stream transport error: unexpected EOF`.\n   Retryable.\n4. **Transport error**: `fetch` rejected or the body read failed for a\n   network reason (connection refused/reset, DNS failure, socket closed,\n   TLS failure, HTTP/2 stream reset, unexpected EOF mid-body). Retryable.\n5. **Abort**: the request's `AbortSignal` fired (caller cancellation, the\n   agent loop's work deadline, or the per-request timeout). Never retried.\n   The adapter rethrows the signal's reason unchanged so the caller can tell\n   them apart.\n6. **Capture error** (2.11). Permanent; never retried, and it disables\n   the client.\n7. **Protocol error**: malformed event JSON, a non-`function` chat tool\n   call type. Not retryable.\n\nRetry delay hints (consumed by the agent loop's retry policy, which owns\nthe loop: up to `maxAttempts` attempts per model call, Go Fantasy\n`DefaultRetryOptions` initial delay 5000 ms, factor 2, so 5 s, 10 s, 20 s):\nfor an HTTP error with headers, `retry-after-ms` (float milliseconds), else\n`retry-after` (float seconds, or an RFC 1123 date relative to now) gives\n`hint`; the delay is `hint` when `hint > 0` and (`hint < 60 s` or `hint <\nbackoff`), otherwise the exponential backoff. Adapters never retry\ninternally (Go disables SDK retries: a 500 with `maxAttempts: 1` reaches\nthe server exactly once).\n\n`normalizeProviderError(outerSignal, model, err)` maps any error that\nescapes the agent loop, in this order:\n\n1. `outerSignal.aborted` -> return `outerSignal.reason` (caller\n   cancellation passes through untouched).\n2. `err` is an abort or timeout (request timeout, work-deadline-bounded\n   call) -> `ErrEndpoint` with message\n   `llm: inference endpoint failure: <model>: <err message>`, keeping the\n   timeout as `cause` (pinned: a request timeout is an endpoint failure that\n   still identifies as a deadline).\n3. `err` already is `ErrAuth`, `ErrEndpoint`, or `ErrBudgetExhausted`\n   (ledger area) -> unchanged.\n4. `err` carries HTTP status 401 or 403 anywhere in its cause chain ->\n   `ErrAuth`: `llm: authentication failed: <err message>; check the\n   configured API key`.\n5. Otherwise -> `ErrEndpoint` as in step 2.\n\nSentinel kinds (Go `errors.go`) become error classes with a `kind` field\nso callers test `err instanceof AuthError` or walk `cause`:\n`ErrNoFinalCall` (`llm: tool loop ended without a final tool call`),\n`ErrWorkDeadline` (`llm: work deadline reached`), `ErrAuth`\n(`llm: authentication failed`), `ErrEndpoint`\n(`llm: inference endpoint failure`). The first two are raised by the agent\nloop; they are defined here so the whole `llm` error vocabulary lives in\none module.\n\n### 2.11 Raw response capture\n8-pure unit tests for the SSE parser, usage normalization and encoders.\n9-A shared fixture writer ports `testutil.WriteInferenceStream`: from a\n10:complete response object it emits the native SSE sequence for each\n11:protocol (chat chunks plus `[DONE]`; responses events with\n12-`sequence_number`; anthropic `message_start` ... `message_stop`).\n13-\n14-Wire shape and headers:\n15-\n16-- Anthropic posts to `<base>/v1/messages` after `/v1` trimming, sends\n17-  `X-Api-Key`, a non-empty `Anthropic-Version`, `system`, `stream: true`,\n--\n23-- Anthropic and structured calls use `tool_choice.type == \"auto\"`\n24-  (`TestAnthropicCompleteStructuredUsesAutomaticToolChoice`) (C).\n25:- Responses replays `function_call_output`, sends `store: false`, no\n26:  `previous_response_id`, `tool_choice: \"auto\"`, identical tools on the\n27:  final turn (`TestResponsesAgentReplaysToolOutputAndKeepsToolsOnFinalTurn`)\n28-  (C).\n29-- Tool schemas reach each protocol with `additionalProperties` and nested\n30-  `required` lists intact\n31-  (`TestToolSchemasCarryRequiredFields`) (C).\n32-- `User-Agent` is `roast/<version>` (`TestUserAgentIncludesBuildVersion`)\n33-  (U on the header builder).\n34-- Chat `max_completion_tokens` for reasoning-model IDs, `max_tokens`\n35:  otherwise; responses system mode by model (no Go test; new) (U).\n36-\n37-Ambient environment and credentials:\n38-\n39-- For each protocol and each env scenario (provider keys, auth token,\n40-  explicit and fallback Anthropic profile, federation, custom headers),\n41-  only the configured endpoint is called, once, with only Roast headers\n--\n45-- Anthropic 401 maps to `AuthError`\n46-  (`TestAnthropicMapsAuthenticationFailure`) (C, exit code and JSON).\n47:- A 3xx from any protocol (`chat`, `responses`, `anthropic`) is not\n48-  followed, the target sees no key, and the error is an `EndpointError`,\n49-  not retried (`TestAnthropicDoesNotForwardCredentialsThroughRedirect`,\n50-  extended) (A).\n51-- An error body larger than 32 KiB is read only up to 32768 bytes (new)\n52-  (A).\n53-\n--\n69-  (C via a run-record write failure, or A).\n70-- `Content-Length: 16777217` fails with the size error\n71:  (`TestCaptureRejectsOversizedProviderResponse`) (A).\n72-- Invalid JSON 2xx body fails once, not retried\n73:  (`TestCaptureDoesNotRetryInvalidJSONResponse`) (A).\n74-- Streaming capture does not read ahead, preserves exactly the bytes read,\n75-  releases the body once (`TestStreamCaptureDoesNotEagerlyReadAndPreserves\n76-  PartialBytes`) (A with a controlled `ReadableStream`).\n77-- No `Content-Length`: overflow fails, callback not called, buffer never\n78-  exceeds the cap (`TestStreamCaptureEnforcesLimitWithoutContentLength`)\n79-  (U on `capture.ts`).\n--\n82-  completed calls\n83-  (`TestAnthropicInterruptedStreamRetriesWithoutExecutingPartialTools`)\n84:  (C, run-record raw responses).\n85-\n86-Retries and errors:\n87-\n88-- A 500 with `maxAttempts: 1` reaches the server once for chat and\n89:  responses (`TestChatRetriesOnlyThroughFantasy`,\n90:  `TestResponsesRetriesOnlyThroughFantasy`) (C).\n91-- Request timeout yields `EndpointError` caused by a timeout within one\n92-  second (`TestInferenceRequestTimeoutIsEndpointFailure`) (A).\n93-- Classification table: 408/409/429/5xx/`x-should-retry` retryable,\n94-  401/403/3xx/400 not, transient stream types, incomplete stream,\n95-  transport errors, aborts (new) (U).\n96-- `retryDelayMs` with `retry-after-ms`, `retry-after` seconds and date,\n--\n103-- Stage 2 on 8/4/1/3 -> 8/4/1/3 (`TestGenericUsageAccounting`, updated)\n104-  (U).\n105:- Chat and responses from fixture usage objects: `prompt_tokens: 100,\n106-  cached_tokens: 30` -> uncached 70, cached 30; cached 80 -> 20 and 80 (new)\n107-  (U).\n108-- A chat chunk without usage after a chunk with usage keeps the earlier\n109-  usage (new) (U).\n110-- `encodeToolResult` sorts keys and leaves `<>&` and U+2028 unescaped; a\n111-  lone surrogate in model output decodes to U+FFFD (new) (U).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GmUe5XB1VTFVHaqrNVXCGp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
