{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017uMFMgrxXyq7BrCvYWUGJp","type":"tool_result","content":"13:897-`[event: <name>\\n]data: <json>\\n\\n`. For `responses`, every emitted\n14-898-object gets `sequence_number` 0, 1, 2, ... in emission order.\n15-899-\n16-900-- `anthropic`: `message_start` with `message` = response with `content:\n17-901-  []`, `stop_reason: null`, `usage` copied with `output_tokens: 0`. For\n18-902-  each content block at index i: `content_block_start` (`index`,\n19-903-  `content_block` = block with `thinking` and `signature` emptied for\n20-904-  thinking, `text` emptied for text, `input: {}` for tool use); deltas\n21-905-  (`thinking_delta` + `signature_delta`; `text_delta`; or\n22-906-  `input_json_delta` with `partial_json` = JSON of the input);\n23-907-  `content_block_stop`. Then `message_delta` (`delta: {stop_reason,\n24-908-  stop_sequence: null}`, `usage` = response usage) and `message_stop`.\n25-909-  Event name = the object's `type`.\n26:910-- `responses`: `response.created` (`response` with `output: []`,\n27-911-  `status: in_progress`); per output item: `response.output_item.added`\n28-912-  (item with `arguments: \"\"`, `status: in_progress`),\n29-913-  `response.function_call_arguments.delta` (`item_id`, `delta` =\n30-914-  arguments), `response.function_call_arguments.done` (`arguments`),\n31-915-  `response.output_item.done` (full item), each with `output_index`;\n32-916-  then `response.completed` with the full response.\n33-917-- `chat`: no `event:` lines. Three chunks, each `{id, object:\n34-918-  \"chat.completion.chunk\", created: 1, model, choices}`: first, choices\n35-919-  with `delta` = message with `tool_calls` re-indexed (`index` = position)\n36-920-  and `finish_reason: null`; second, choices with empty `delta` and the\n37-921-  real `finish_reason`; third, `choices: []` plus `usage`. Then\n38-922-  `data: [DONE]\\n\\n`.\n39-923-\n40-924-## 4. Deliberate changes\n41-925-\n42-926-1. The cobra `completion` command is dropped.\n43-927-2. Windows is not supported: `openBrowser` uses `open` (darwin) or\n44-928-   `xdg-open` (linux) only.\n45-929-3. Node `>=22.18`, checked at startup; below it the CLI prints a clear\n46-930-   error and exits 2 (spec.md change 3).\n47-931-4. Debug tracing via `@substrate-system/debug` namespace `roast:cli`\n48-932-   (`DEBUG=roast:*`), never including request/response bodies, headers,\n49-933-   prompts, or credentials.\n50-934-5. First TypeScript release is `2.0.0`; build info comes from esbuild\n51-935-   defines instead of Go ldflags / `debug.ReadBuildInfo`.\n52-936-6. Help text wording and layout come from yargs and need not match\n53-937-   cobra.\n54-938-7. A second SIGINT or SIGTERM force-exits with status 130; Go ignored\n55-939-   repeats (spec.md change 22). Ctrl-C (`\\x03`) at a raw-mode secret prompt\n56-940-   is cancellation, exit 5.\n57-941-8. Accepted yargs parsing differences: decimal-only integers, `--quick\n58-942-   false` read as a value, plain comma splitting of list flags (spec.md\n59-943-   \"CLI parsing\").\n60-944-9. JSON error output is not HTML-escaped; parity is on parsed JSON.\n61-945-10. EPIPE on stdout exits quietly with the computed code instead of dying\n62-946-    by SIGPIPE.\n63-947-11. A parse failure reports in the parsed `--error-format` when yargs\n64-948-    produced one, else text.\n65-949-\n66-950-Not a change: the gate bootstrap's terminal check uses the swappable\n// Fixture writer for fake inference servers (spec 01, 3.8; Go\n// testutil.WriteInferenceStream): from a complete response object, emit\n// the protocol's native SSE stream. Only `chat` exists so far; the\n// `responses` and `anthropic` formats join it in later tickets.\n\n// The part of `http.ServerResponse` the writer uses.\nexport interface StreamSink {\n    setHeader (name:string, value:string):unknown;\n    write (chunk:string):unknown;\n    end ():unknown;\n}\n\ntype Json = Record<string, unknown>\n\nfunction obj (v:unknown):Json {\n    return v !== null && typeof v === 'object' && !Array.isArray(v) ?\n        v as Json :\n        {}\n}\n\nfunction event (data:unknown, name?:string):string {\n    const head = name ? `event: ${name}\\n` : ''\n    const body = typeof data === 'string' ? data : JSON.stringify(data)\n    return `${head}data: ${body}\\n\\n`\n}\n\n// Three chunks (delta, finish, usage) and `[DONE]`.\nfunction chatEvents (response:Json):string[] {\n    const base = {\n        id:response.id,\n        object:'chat.completion.chunk',\n        created:1,\n        model:response.model,\n    }\n    const choices = Array.isArray(response.choices) ? response.choices : []\n    const deltas = choices.map((c:unknown) => {\n        const choice = obj(c)\n        const delta = { ...obj(choice.message) }\n        if (Array.isArray(delta.tool_calls)) {\n            delta.tool_calls = delta.tool_calls.map((tc:unknown, i:number) => (\n                { ...obj(tc), index:i }\n            ))\n        }\n        return { index:choice.index, delta, finish_reason:null }\n    })\n    const finishes = choices.map((c:unknown) => {\n        const choice = obj(c)\n        return {\n            index:choice.index,\n            delta:{},\n            finish_reason:choice.finish_reason,\n        }\n    })\n    return [\n        event({ ...base, choices:deltas }),\n        event({ ...base, choices:finishes }),\n        event({ ...base, choices:[], usage:response.usage }),\n        event('[DONE]'),\n    ]\n}\n\nexport function writeInferenceStream (\n    res:StreamSink,\n    protocol:string,\n    response:unknown\n):void {\n    let events:string[]\n    if (protocol === 'chat') events = chatEvents(obj(response))\n    else throw new Error(`unsupported inference protocol \"${protocol}\"`)\n    res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/event-stream')\n    for (const e of events) res.write(e)\n    res.end()\n}\n\n// `writeInferenceStream` from a JSON string.\nexport function writeJSONStream (\n    res:StreamSink,\n    protocol:string,\n    body:string\n):void {\n    writeInferenceStream(res, protocol, JSON.parse(body))\n}\n// A `node:http` fake inference server (Go httptest plus providerServer):\n// it records every request and answers from a script that looks at the\n// request (path, body, headers) and the request's position.\nimport {\n    createServer,\n    type IncomingHttpHeaders,\n    type ServerResponse,\n} from 'node:http'\nimport type { AddressInfo } from 'node:net'\nimport { writeInferenceStream } from './inference-stream.js'\n\nexport interface RecordedRequest {\n    method:string;\n    path:string;\n    headers:IncomingHttpHeaders;\n    // Header names and values exactly as sent, in order.\n    rawHeaders:string[];\n    rawBody:Buffer;\n    // The parsed JSON body; undefined when it is not JSON.\n    body:unknown;\n}\n\nexport type Reply =\n    // A complete response object, streamed in the protocol's SSE format;\n    // the protocol defaults to the one the request path implies.\n    | { stream:unknown, protocol?:string }\n    | { status:number, headers?:Record<string, string>, body?:string|Buffer }\n    // Full control: write the response yourself.\n    | ((res:ServerResponse, req:RecordedRequest) => void|Promise<void>)\n\n// Picks the reply for the n-th request (0-based).\nexport type Script = (req:RecordedRequest, n:number) => Reply\n\nexport interface InferenceServer {\n    // `http://127.0.0.1:<port>`.\n    url:string;\n    requests:RecordedRequest[];\n    close ():Promise<void>;\n}\n\nexport function protocolForPath (path:string):string {\n    if (path.endsWith('/chat/completions')) return 'chat'\n    if (path.endsWith('/responses')) return 'responses'\n    if (path.endsWith('/v1/messages')) return 'anthropic'\n    return ''\n}\n\nasync function reply (res:ServerResponse, req:RecordedRequest, r:Reply) {\n    if (typeof r === 'function') {\n        await r(res, req)\n        return\n    }\n    if ('stream' in r) {\n        writeInferenceStream(res, r.protocol ?? protocolForPath(req.path),\n            r.stream)\n        return\n    }\n    res.writeHead(r.status, r.headers ?? {})\n    res.end(r.body ?? '')\n}\n\nexport async function startInferenceServer (\n    script:Script\n):Promise<InferenceServer> {\n    const requests:RecordedRequest[] = []\n    const server = createServer((req, res) => {\n        const parts:Buffer[] = []\n        req.on('data', (c:Buffer) => parts.push(c))\n        req.on('end', () => {\n            const rawBody = Buffer.concat(parts)\n            let body:unknown\n            try {\n                body = JSON.parse(rawBody.toString('utf8'))\n            } catch {\n                body = undefined\n            }\n            const rec:RecordedRequest = {\n                method:req.method ?? '',\n                path:req.url ?? '',\n                headers:req.headers,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3b53f31-1a37-4344-81e1-3cd017cb5d08","uuid":"ac8fec21-bbf8-4c4e-8e33-2e703ce5d272","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:46:51.304Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"13:897-`[event: <name>\\n]data: <json>\\n\\n`. For `responses`, every emitted\n14-898-object gets `sequence_number` 0, 1, 2, ... in emission order.\n15-899-\n16-900-- `anthropic`: `message_start` with `message` = response with `content:\n17-901-  []`, `stop_reason: null`, `usage` copied with `output_tokens: 0`. For\n18-902-  each content block at index i: `content_block_start` (`index`,\n19-903-  `content_block` = block with `thinking` and `signature` emptied for\n20-904-  thinking, `text` emptied for text, `input: {}` for tool use); deltas\n21-905-  (`thinking_delta` + `signature_delta`; `text_delta`; or\n22-906-  `input_json_delta` with `partial_json` = JSON of the input);\n23-907-  `content_block_stop`. Then `message_delta` (`delta: {stop_reason,\n24-908-  stop_sequence: null}`, `usage` = response usage) and `message_stop`.\n25-909-  Event name = the object's `type`.\n26:910-- `responses`: `response.