{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM1DuvuGKNxLeo624nBY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0188HZuqSF5m2SL7KQyp7Xhb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/agents/llm.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- Tool results sent to models go through `encodeToolResult` (`json.ts`)\n  only.\"\"\",\"\"\"- Tool results sent to models go through `encodeToolResult` (`json.ts`)\n  only.\n- Usage stage 1 lives in `usage.ts` per protocol (`chatUsage`,\n  `responsesUsage`); decoders call `normalizeUsage` on its result.\n- Making an adapter available changes tests that pin unavailability:\n  the construction test in `test/llm/client.ts` and the doctor roundtrip\n  test (`test/cli/doctor.ts`, whose `doctorProbe` must speak the\n  protocol).\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  native SSE per protocol).\"\"\",\"\"\"  native SSE per protocol). The `responses` writer, like Go's, emits\n  every output item as a function call, so message items yield no text.\n- CLI review tests on `responses` use `responsesProfileConfig`,\n  `responsesFindingsReply`, and `responsesCalls` (`test/helpers/review.ts`).\n  Requests through `runRoast`'s rewriting fetch carry\n  `transfer-encoding`; filter it with the other transport headers.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/agents/typescript.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- Review scenarios script the fake with `scriptedServer`\"\"\",\"\"\"- Review scenarios are protocol-parametrized: `review(case, protocol)`\n  in `scenarios/m3.ts`; M4 (`scenarios/m4.ts`) reruns the M3 cases on\n  `responses`, rewriting chat replies with `responsesFromChat`.\n- Review scenarios script the fake with `scriptedServer`\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -nP '[^\\x00-\\x7f]' docs/agents/llm.md docs/agents/typescript.md; cat >> .redeye/notes.md <<'EOF'\n- src/llm/client.ts: `responses` entry in ADAPTERS.\n- test/llm/responses-http.ts (adapter seam: endpoint/headers/env, 3xx,\n  replay + same tools on final turn, incomplete-stream retry,\n  failed/error not retried, capture). Red: \"unsupported protocol\".\n- Updated pinned-unavailability tests: test/llm/client.ts construction\n  (responses now ok; anthropic still unsupported), test/cli/doctor.ts\n  roundtrip (responses now passes; doctorProbe speaks responses).\n- test/cli/review-responses.ts (CLI seam): exit 0/1, report shape equals\n  chat's, wire shape incl. full schemas + strict:false, --max-attempts 1\n  500 once (exit 4 endpoint), length finish not dispatched (exit 4,\n  one request, no function_call_output), meta usage 70/30 and 20/80,\n  ambient OPENAI_*/OPENROUTER_* in io.env add nothing, 3xx endpoint\n  error target untouched, provider-responses.jsonl body byte-for-byte.\n  These passed on first run because the adapter seam went red first.\n- test/diff/scenarios/m4.ts + selftest/m4.ts; m3.ts parametrized by\n  protocol (`review(case, protocol)`, names get \" (responses)\").\n\n## BLOCKER: harness acceptance item (same as ticket 26)\nGo is on PATH here. `npm run test:diff`: all self-tests pass; the 8 M3\nand 8 M4 Go comparisons fail on exactly one difference each: TS sends\nthe `__roast_continue` nudge tool in `body.tools`, Go never does (spec\n07 \"Open questions\" 1, undecided). No other difference in any responses\nscenario (exit codes, stdout JSON, records, other request fields agree).\nNot allowlisted (no numbered deliberate change). Once the maintainer\ndecides, the M4 scenarios need nothing extra.\n\n## Reading of criteria\n- \"posts to <base>/v1/responses\": base is the fake server URL; profile\n  endpoint is `<url>/v1`, request URL is `<endpoint>/responses`.\n- rawFinishReason is set whenever incomplete_details.reason is non-empty.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":170450,"cache_creation":{"ephemer