alse`, `stream: true`, `tool_choice: \"auto\"`, and no `previous_response_id`. The final (wrap-up) turn carries the same tools as earlier turns. A tool result is replayed as a `function_call_output` item with the matching `call_id`.\n[x] Each tool definition reaches the endpoint with `parameters` equal to the caller's full JSON Schema, including `additionalProperties` and nested `required`, plus `strict: false`.\n[x] `responsesSystemMode` returns `system` for IDs matching `gpt-3|gpt-4|chatgpt-|-chat`, `remove` for `o1-mini` / `o1-preview`, and `developer` otherwise. The encoded `input` reflects that mode (unit).\n[x] With `maxAttempts: 1`, a 500 reaches the server exactly once (CLI seam, exit and JSON error category).\n[x] `response.failed` and `error` events fail the call without a retry. A stream that ends with neither `response.completed` nor `response.incomplete` is retried as an incomplete stream (adapter seam).\n[x] Finish mapping: absent or empty reason -> `tool-calls` or `stop`; `max_output_tokens` -> `length`; `content_filter` -> `content-filter`. Tool calls on a `length` finish are never dispatched (CLI seam: the fake records no follow-up turn carrying their output).\n[x] Usage from a fixture with `input_tokens: 100` and 30 cached tokens lands in `meta.json` as 70 uncached and 30 cached. With 80 cached, it is 20 and 80.\n[x] Ambient `OPENAI_*` / `OPENROUTER_*` variables, and any header variables in `io.env`, add no headers or credentials to a `responses` request. A 3xx is not followed, its target sees no key, and the error is an endpoint error.\n[x] Each raw `text/event-stream` body appears byte-for-byte in the run's `provider-responses.jsonl` with protocol `responses`.\n[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\nI left one item unchecked: the harness item (\"Go and TS agree on exit code, parsed JSON stdout, requests grouped by (model, turn count), and run records\"). It's blocked by the same thing that blocked ticket 26.\n\n**Harness blocker:** the 8 new `responses` scenarios now run against the Go baseline. Each one fails on exactly one difference: TS sends the `__roast_continue` nudge tool in `body.tools` and Go never does. The 8 existing chat scenarios fail the same way. Nothing else differs in any `responses` scenario: exit codes, stdout JSON, run records and every other request field all match. Whether TS should drop the nudge tool or the difference should become a numbered deliberate change is open question 1 in spec 07, and that's your call. I didn't allowlist it or change the agent loop. Once you decide, the M4 scenarios need no further work. Without Go, `npm run test:diff` passes all its self-tests, including 4 new M4 ones that run the TS CLI against itself.\n\n**What was built:**\n- **The adapter** (`src/llm/responses.ts`): request encoding and stream decoding follow spec 06 2.6.2 and 2.8.2. Token counts subtract cached tokens once (`responsesUsage` in `usage.ts`). `client.ts` now sends `responses` profiles to it; nothing in the agent loop is protocol-specific.\n- **Fake server**: `writeInferenceStream` now writes the `responses` event sequence, numbering events in order as Go does.\n- **Tests** at three levels: unit (`test/llm/responses.ts`), the adapter against the fake server (`test/llm/responses-http.ts`), and full CLI reviews (`test/cli/review-responses.ts`).\n- **Harness**: `scenarios/m3.ts` now takes a protocol, and `scenarios/m4.ts` reruns the M3 cases on `responses`.\n\n**Behaviour choices to check:**\n- The decoder keeps reading after the final event so the recorded response contains every byte.\n- `rawFinishReason` is set whenever the provider gives a non-empty `incomplete_details.reason`.\n\n**Two existing tests changed**, because they asserted that `responses` was unavailable: the construction test in `test/llm/client.ts` (it now checks `anthropic` instead), and the doctor round-trip test, whose fake server can now answer `responses` requests.\n\n**Test-first:** the CLI-level tests passed on their first run. The test-first failures happened one level down, at the adapter and unit tests, before `client.ts` handled `responses`. For the pure encoder and decoder, I wrote the tests and code together because the spec fixes the exact shape. Both points are in `.redeye/notes.md`.\n\nI also added notes on this area to `docs/agents/llm.md` and `docs/agents/typescript.md`. Everything is committed except `.redeye/notes.md`.","ttft_ms":1291,"type":"result","duration_ms":910953,"uuid":"b83514b5-177b-4d71-a585-3629cb2e71a8","ttft_stream_ms":1045,"time_to_request_ms":156,"first_content_frame_ms":1046,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":138,"outputTokens":45458,"cacheReadInputTokens":8857143,"cacheCreationInputTokens":162679,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.9825726,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":8191,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":162679,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-09T10:07:39.368Z"}
